---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy">
  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="wrap"><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="lede">Last Updated: September 2026</p></div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="card legal-content">
        <h3>1. Introduction and Scope</h3>
        <p>JECON LLC ("we," "our," or "us") respects the privacy of our clients, partners, and website visitors, including users of the JECON Platform. This Privacy Policy outlines our data collection, use, and protection practices, tailored to our role as a federal services provider, government contractor, and software provider.</p>
        <p>By accessing or using our website, the JECON Platform, or our services, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by the terms of this Privacy Policy.</p>

        <h3>2. Information We Collect</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Personal Identification Information:</strong> Name, email address, phone number, job title, and organization name when you voluntarily provide it through our contact forms, consultation scheduling tools, or JECON Platform account creation.</li>
          <li><strong>Technical Data:</strong> IP address, browser type and version, time zone setting, and operating system, collected automatically to maintain site and platform stability and to defend against cyber threats.</li>
          <li><strong>Contracting Data:</strong> For potential partners and subcontractors, we may collect capability statements, CAGE codes, and UEI numbers submitted for teaming arrangements.</li>
          <li><strong>JECON Platform Account & Usage Data:</strong> Organization name, account type, services of interest, plan tier, and payment preference collected at signup; documents you upload (lists of materials, invoices, proof-of-delivery, insurance certificates, and similar records) and the data extracted from them; and records of actions you and our AI features take within your account.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>3. How We Use Your Information</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Responding to inquiries regarding program management, logistics, and administrative support services.</li>
          <li>Evaluating potential teaming arrangements or sub-contracting capabilities for federal and commercial solicitations.</li>
          <li>Operating your JECON Platform account: authenticating sign-in, provisioning your workspace, and providing the features you've signed up for.</li>
          <li>Complying with statutory reporting requirements, defense procurement guidelines, and operational security protocols.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell, trade, rent, or otherwise disseminate your personal information to third parties for marketing purposes.</p>

        <h3>4. AI-Assisted Features</h3>
        <p>The JECON Platform uses AI to read uploaded documents, extract structured data, detect variances, and draft proposals such as reorders, hand receipts, and settlements. These AI outputs are suggestions only — nothing is finalized, ordered, or transferred until a person in your organization reviews and approves it. Every AI-proposed action and every human approval or rejection is recorded in an audit trail tied to your account.</p>
        <p>Documents and data you submit to AI features are processed to generate results for your account and are not used to train models for other customers.</p>

        <h3>5. No Controlled or Classified Data</h3>
        <p>The JECON Platform is not designed, at this time, to receive or store controlled unclassified information (CUI), export-controlled data (e.g., ITAR/EAR), or classified information of any kind. Please do not upload such material to the platform. Support for controlled data handling is planned for a later phase and will be announced separately.</p>

        <h3>6. Government & Compliance Data</h3>
        <p>As a government contractor, we adhere to strict data handling protocols. Data exchanged in connection with federal contracts is handled in accordance with applicable federal regulations, including DFARS 252.204-7012, NIST SP 800-171, and CMMC cybersecurity frameworks, to the extent applicable to that engagement.</p>

        <h3>7. Data Security</h3>
        <p>We implement administrative, technical, and physical security measures to protect data against unauthorized access, destruction, or interception. JECON Platform accounts and data are protected by Row Level Security at the database layer, so access is restricted to your own organization's data by default. Access is otherwise limited to authorized personnel with a legitimate business need.</p>

        <h3>8. Third-Party Services</h3>
        <p>We use third-party infrastructure providers (including Supabase for authentication and data storage, and Stripe for payment processing) and link to select third-party services (such as LinkedIn and Calendly). We do not control their independent privacy practices and encourage you to review the terms of any external platform you use.</p>

        <h3>9. JECON Platform Accounts</h3>
        <p>If you create a JECON Platform account, we collect the information you provide (name, email, organization, account type, and selected services) to set up your workspace and communicate with you about the service. Documents you upload are used to provide the service to you, and AI features process those documents to generate proposals that you review. We do not sell your account data or uploaded documents.</p>

        <h3>10. Contact Information</h3>
        <p>If you have questions about this policy or our data practices, contact us at <strong>info@jeconllc.com</strong> or via mail at our Sierra Vista headquarters.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
